  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_nicholsi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Schistura nicholsi, the Redtail Zebra Sand Loach, belongs to an unusually large genus of about 200 species. Adults reach approximately 9 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_nicholsi_en/",
      "html": "<p>It originates from the Mekong basin in Thailand and Laos.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_nicholsi_en/",
      "html": "<p>It inhabits fast flowing waters on a stony ground.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_nicholsi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Tanks of 1 m length are sufficiently large for a group of at least 5 animals.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_nicholsi_en/",
      "html": "<p>To ensure a high oxygen content and a sufficient current in the aquarium, it should have an efficient filter. With pebbles in different sizes and some roots you can try to arrange a bank seam in the aquarium. The fish accept this enthusiastically and are always investigating and searching for food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_nicholsi_en/",
      "html": "<p>They like living insect larvae most, but can be accustomed without any problems to frozen and also flake food.</p>"
    }
  ],
